            <div xml:id="d425-a2">

                <pb facs="0799" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg689"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 483.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pratt to Colonel
                            Stewart.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 8,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the closing paragraph of
                    your dispatch No. 42 of the 2d instant, concerning the difficulty about the
                    house at Khoi, treated of in the letter you inclosed me from Mr. J. C. Mechlin,
                    I have to express to you my thanks for bringing the matter in dispute so
                    promptly to the attention of the authorities at Tabreez, and trust that you will
                    be able to satisfactorily arrange the affair with the Emir Nizam, on the spot,
                    without having to refer it here for settlement.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Spencer Pratt.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
